  "title": "Reject non-finite --min-age in cleanup-grid-sessions.py",
  "body": "> Fixes #\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\nNot required, development only.\n\n## Description\n\nFollow-up to #5880, from [this review comment](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/pull/5880#discussion_r4301102174).\n\n`cleanup-grid-sessions.py --min-age` uses `type=float`, so it accepts `nan` and `inf`. The old check only rejected negative values:\n\n- `--min-age nan` passed, and because `age < nan` is always false, the script deleted every session with a known start time, including young sessions of other runs on a shared grid.\n- `--min-age inf` (or `1e400`) passed and kept every session, which is never what the caller wants.\n\nThe script now rejects any value that is not a finite number of seconds, zero or more, before it contacts the grid.\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- `cleanup-grid-sessions.py`: validate `--min-age` with `math.isfinite()` in addition to the negative check, with the error `--min-age must be a finite number of seconds, zero or more`\n\nVerified against a fake grid status server on a local port (one 10-second-old session, one 1000-second-old session, one with unknown start time), logging every request:\n\n- `nan`, `NaN`, `inf`, `-inf`, `Infinity`, `1e400`, `-1`, `-0.5`: exit code 2 with the error, no HTTP request\n- `0`, `400`, `400 --dry-run`, `--dry-run`, and no option: same output and requests as before\n\n- [ ] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [ ] I have updated `CHANGELOG.md`\n- [ ] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n",
